::JOUR_U01_L04_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Scenario: A digital story places the verified schedule at the top and decoration below it. What design principle is being used? {
=A. Design hierarchy that prioritizes important information#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. Random decoration#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Hidden sourcing#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. Fictional layout#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_GP_Q02::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.03] A photo caption is accurate when it: {
~A. adds a dramatic claim not shown in the image#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. truthfully identifies and explains the image#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~C. hides who is pictured#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. replaces verified facts#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_GP_Q03::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Which design choice best supports a mobile audience? {
~A. Dense paragraphs in tiny type#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. Unlabeled photos#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. Short verified bullet points and a link to the full story#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. Unrelated graphics#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_GP_Q04::[MLA.JOUR.ETH.01] A design choice meets format-specific quality when it: {
~A. looks exciting even if misleading#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. uses no captions#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. hides the main facts#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=D. supports accurate information in the chosen format#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_GP_Q05::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Which statement best separates design from decoration in journalism? {
=A. Design should help the audience understand verified information.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. Design only needs bright colors.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Decoration is more important than facts.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. Captions are optional in journalism.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
